A||N||8||whamel||License plate question||||5||
Z||000000||whamel||09-19-2000||10:58 AM||||Okay - I was looking through some old posts here about custom plates and such (just got approved for mine for the GT) and noticed most of the posts of pictures are followed up by someone saying something like 'hasn't anyone told you the risks of posting your plate on the net.'  Forgive me for pulling a Duh! here, but what's the problem with posting your plate on the net?<BR>Thanks,<BR>Wade<BR>P.S. Please be specific, I'm obviously in my 'stupid phase' this week.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||09-19-2000||11:19 AM||||Well, someone who know's someone who knows someone who has connections with a police officer could run your plate and get your name, number, address and any other goodie goodie info about you.  I'm pretty sure this is the reason why it's not recommended.  For the most part it probably isn't anything too worry about, but why take any chances.||||reg||1
Z||000002||whamel||09-19-2000||01:04 PM||||I figured it was something like that - wasn't sure if there was anything else involved with it as well though.  I'm not terribly worried about people running my information - if they wanted to know where I lived or whatever there are lots easier ways than that.<BR>I've had people stop by my house and complain about my speeding and my aggressive driving before.  IMHO - that's a not a good thing to do.  I don't take kindly to them thar trespassers.<BR>Now I just have to get one of them fancy sig lines and I'll be all set!<BR>Thanks,<BR>Wade<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||09-19-2000||06:36 PM||||Dave Gray<BR>283 N. Thorne St.<BR>Wabash, IN  46992<BR>unlisted phone #<BR>Plates say, "MNKY MAN".<P>(Just thought this might save someone the trouble. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000004||whamel||09-19-2000||07:30 PM||||By the way, my plate is: HAUNTD - fitting if you've looked at my car I'd say.<BR>Later,<BR>Wade||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||09-19-2000||10:02 PM||||I can see why people are concerned, except that anybody near your car can pick up the info anyway.  So unless you flame someone online who turns out to be a serial killer or something, I wouldn't worry too much about it.  I am thinking of getting personalized plates too... just waiting for NY to come out with the new style.  I think October is the first month but I am not positive.  (YEAH!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> No more red statue!)<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/Motorcity/Boulevard/9278/fierosig1.jpg">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000006||HugGRRRFiero||09-19-2000||10:30 PM||||I like Monkeyman's Plate!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I can hear the report over the police scanner now.  <P>Indiana State Trooper:<BR>&lt;sirens blazing&gt;<BR>Yea, Do you copy?... we're in hot pursuit of a purple Fiero going north on I-69 at a high rate of speed...  License plate M.N.K.Y.M.A.N.<P>Radio Dispatch:<BR>Ok, who let this guy out of his cage?  Just let him go, he's probably on his way to a Fiero show  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>That is too cool!<P>I should get one that says HUGGRRR  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000007||whamel||09-19-2000||10:37 PM||||You know - I was driving through Ft. Wayne on Sunday and I saw this purple Pontiac (non-fiero) with a big ape sticker on the back window that said KONG under it.  Kind made me think of MM a little bit.  Of course, I have no idea where Wabash is, but I probably drive through there twice a week for all I know.  I autopilot my 350 mile commute now pretty much.<BR>Wade<BR>P.S. just checked the map out of curiosity and yes, I do kinda drive by there twice a week every week.  ARGH!  MM, I should have just driven down to your house to pick up those parts!||||reg||1
